
Step 1: Copy the Bookmarklet Code

Copy the exact line of JavaScript below:
javascript
javascript:(function(){var s=document.createElement('script');s.src='https://jsdelivr.net{eruda.init();};})();
Use code with caution.

Step 2: Create the Bookmark

• Bookmark any webpage. Open your mobile or desktop browser, visit any site, and add it to your bookmarks.
• Open your bookmarks list. Go to your browser's bookmarks menu and find the bookmark you just saved.
• Edit the bookmark. Tap Edit on that bookmark and give it a short, easy-to-remember name like Eruda.
• Paste the code. Delete the existing web address in the URL (or Address) field, paste the JavaScript code from Step 1, and save your changes.

Step 3: Open Eruda on Rollscapes

• Load the game. Navigate to the ProtoType Studios Rollscapes page.
• Run the bookmarklet. Tap the browser's address bar at the top or bottom of the screen, type Eruda, and select your bookmark from the dropdown suggestions (do not hit search).
• Open the menu. A floating gear icon will appear on your screen. Tap it to open the developer console.

Step 4: Inspect or Test Changes

• View saved data. Tap the Resources tab inside Eruda, then select Local Storage to see if the game saves progress or scores locally.
• Test custom scripts. Tap the Console tab to type and run JavaScript commands directly on the page (for example, typing Math.random = () => 0.9999; to test maximum roll outputs).
